11.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
Deliberation round 1 achieved unanimous consensus on Option B across all colleagues. The core mechanistic points are established: both (2E)-4-hydroxy-2-nonen-8-ynal and 4-octyl itaconate (4-OI) covalently modify sensor cysteines on Keap1, leading to Nrf2 stabilization and the transcriptional upregulation (increase) of downstream cytoprotective enzymes, including ALDH. While 4-HNE derivatives exhibit higher intrinsic Michael acceptor reactivity, a 50 µM concentration causes severe proteotoxicity and translational attenuation; conversely, 50 µM 4-OI delivers targeted Keap1 alkylation with preserved translational capacity, resulting in a more pronounced net accumulation of ALDH. With all participants converging on Option B, the group position is fully aligned.
}

